    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_2",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "The M1919 Browning is a .30 caliber medium machine gun that was widely used during the 20th century, especially during World War II, the Korean War, and the Vietnam War. The M1919 saw service as a light infantry, coaxial, mounted, aircraft, and anti-aircraft machine gun by the U.S. and many other countries. Many M1919s were rechambered for the new 7.62×51mm NATO round and remain in service to this day.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999954020322,
